Module528910Name = E-invoice check (FacturX API)
Module528910Desc = Checks, from the invoice card, that the e-invoice file is ready to be sent under the official rules.
FacturxVerifyDescription = Checks, from the invoice card, that the e-invoice file is ready to be sent under the official rules.
FacturxVerifyDescriptionLong = This module neither generates nor sends invoices: it checks the file produced by your e-invoicing module (official module, Factur-X, CII) against the official rules (EN 16931 and the French e-invoicing rules), lists what blocks it and can propose a repair.
FacturxVerifyTab = Check
FacturxVerifyTitle = Check the e-invoice before sending it
FacturxVerifyIntro = The selected file is checked against the official rules (EN 16931 and the French e-invoicing rules). Nothing is sent to your certified platform.
FacturxVerifyFile = File
FacturxVerifyKind_cii = CII XML
FacturxVerifyKind_facturx_pdf = Factur-X PDF
FacturxVerifyKind_ubl = UBL XML
FacturxVerifyKind_pdf = PDF without embedded XML
FacturxVerifyCheckButton = Check before sending
FacturxVerifyCheckButtonHelp = Check the e-invoice file against the official rules
FacturxVerifyQuotaNotice = Each check counts as 1 processed invoice on your FacturX API quota (free key: 100 invoices in the first 14 days, then 10 per month).
FacturxVerifyNoFile = No e-invoice file (CII XML, Factur-X PDF or UBL XML) was found in this invoice's documents. Generate it first with your e-invoicing module.
FacturxVerifyNotConfigured = The module is not configured yet: it needs a (free) FacturX API key.
FacturxVerifyGoToSetup = Set up
FacturxVerifyLastResult = Last check
